# The build context is backend/, so every path here is relative to that.
#
# Anything not excluded is uploaded to the daemon on every build and can end up
# in an image layer — and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image,
# including after a later layer deletes the file.

# Secrets. The container is configured by compose `environment:` and `env_file:`
# entries, which set variables at run time and never touch a layer. A .env baked
# into the image would put JWT_SECRET and the database password on disk in it.
#
# This has to be stated here and not left to .gitignore: `COPY . .` sees the
# working directory, not the index, so an untracked .env would still be copied.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Host build output. These are compiled for the host OS and would be copied in
# only to be overwritten by the real build.
bin/
api
api.exe
migrate
migrate.exe
tmp/

# Not needed to compile. The daemon reads Dockerfile and .dockerignore directly
# rather than from the context; *.md matches nothing under backend/ today and is
# listed so that adding a README later cannot invalidate the build cache.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
